      "targeted_symptom": "S020",
      "patient_response": "Oh, boy... I, um... I really hate to admit this. I don't want you to think I'm crazy, Dr. Smith. I'm a good, reliable worker, I promise. But... well, yes. I guess I have been hearing some things. \n\nI try to just brush it off as stress, you know? But sometimes, even when I'm just sitting out in my own garage at home, with the truck off and everything completely quiet... I hear the dispatch voices. Just as clear as day. They, um... they call out my operator number. And they say that I'm dangerous, or that security is coming to get me. \n\nIt's probably just my mind playing tricks on me from being around the loud equipment so much, or just being overtired, right? I mean, does that sound like something that happens when a person is just under a whole lot of pressure? I really hope it's okay that I shared that with you, I just want to make sure I'm giving you the right answers.",
